            <fr:title text="The entrywise Frobenius">The entrywise Frobenius</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>definition</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">foundations</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">distilled.tex Part 1; journal sec:setup.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>For <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[M \in  \mathrm {M}_n(K)]]></fr:tex>, write <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F(M)]]></fr:tex> for the <html:em>entrywise
Frobenius</html:em> <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(m_{ij}) \mapsto  (m_{ij}^q)]]></fr:tex>. Then <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F]]></fr:tex> is a bijective
ring endomorphism of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathrm {M}_n(K)]]></fr:tex> which preserves and reflects
nilpotency, so <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F(\mathcal {N}) = \mathcal {N}]]></fr:tex>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Mechanism.</html:strong> The <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex>-power map is a ring endomorphism of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[K]]></fr:tex>; its
additivity in characteristic <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[p]]></fr:tex> is what makes it compatible with
matrix multiplication, and it is bijective because Frobenius is
surjective on the algebraically closed <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[K]]></fr:tex>. A bijective ring
endomorphism carries nilpotents to nilpotents both ways.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Role in the skeleton.</html:strong> <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F]]></fr:tex> is the direction in which the whole program deforms.
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0003/" title="The evaluation identity" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0003/" display-uri="ffi-0003" type="local">The evaluation identity</fr:link> reads the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex>-Steenrod operations
off the pencil <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[M + T F(M)]]></fr:tex>, and <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0006/" title="The pencil criterion" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0006/" display-uri="ffi-0006" type="local">the pencil criterion</fr:link>
turns membership in <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[V(J)]]></fr:tex> into nilpotency of every member of
that pencil. It is also the twist that makes <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0011/" title="The trace form" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0011/" display-uri="ffi-0011" type="local">the trace form</fr:link>
identify <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathfrak {gl}_n]]></fr:tex> with its <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F]]></fr:tex>-twisted dual.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0001/" title="Setup: conjugation over a finite field" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0001/" display-uri="ffi-0001" type="local">Setup: conjugation over a finite field</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/sec-foundations/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>sec-foundations</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/sec-foundations/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="finite-field-invariants: a reference forest › Foundations"><fr:link href="/ffi/index/" title="finite-field-invariants: a reference forest" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/index/" display-uri="index" type="local">finite-field-invariants: a reference forest</fr:link> › Foundations</fr:title>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>From the conjugation action to the statement of the height
  conjecture.</html:p>
            <html:ul><html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0001/" title="Setup: conjugation over a finite field" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0001/" display-uri="ffi-0001" type="local">The setup</fr:link> — the ambient objects, the conjugation
    action, and why it is modular.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0054/" title="The characteristic polynomial coefficients" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0054/" display-uri="ffi-0054" type="local">The characteristic polynomial coefficients</fr:link> — the
    <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex> invariants the whole program takes as input.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0055/" title="The entrywise Frobenius" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0055/" display-uri="ffi-0055" type="local">The entrywise Frobenius</fr:link> — the direction everything
    deforms in.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0002/" title="The q-Steenrod operations" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0002/" display-uri="ffi-0002" type="local">The <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex>-Steenrod operations</fr:link> — the operations, and
    what they do to degrees.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0003/" title="The evaluation identity" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0003/" display-uri="ffi-0003" type="local">The evaluation identity</fr:link> — the one fact the program
    runs on.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0004/" title="Polarizations and the trace-form generators" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0004/" display-uri="ffi-0004" type="local">The polarizations</fr:link> — the sparse trace-form
    generators.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0005/" title="The Steenrod ideal" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0005/" display-uri="ffi-0005" type="local">The Steenrod ideal</fr:link> — the ideal whose height is in
    question.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0006/" title="The pencil criterion" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0006/" display-uri="ffi-0006" type="local">The pencil criterion</fr:link> — nilpotency to all orders in
    the Frobenius direction.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0007/" title="Flag witnesses for the partner variety" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0007/" display-uri="ffi-0007" type="local">The flag witnesses</fr:link> — the subvarieties that attain
    the lower bound.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0008/" title="The Krull bound: only the upper bound is open" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0008/" display-uri="ffi-0008" type="local">The Krull bound</fr:link> — why the whole question is an upper
    bound.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0009/" title="The height conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0009/" display-uri="ffi-0009" type="local">The height conjecture</fr:link> — the conjecture itself.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0010/" title="(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0010/" display-uri="ffi-0010" type="local">(*)</fr:link> — what is actually left to prove.</html:li></html:ul>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
